{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790565218649,"sessionID":"ses_f19ff5269ffeWS83Lv5ueXIeyF","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_RREXtZ8f8Ztuq7ADknW6wfsW","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/current_policy.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/current_policy.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Current Finance Travel Policy\n2: \n3: Policy date: 2026-04-20\n4: \n5: Effective for trips starting on or after 2026-05-01. This policy supersedes older travel policy excerpts for covered trips.\n6: \n7: General rules:\n8: \n9: - Use this current policy when it conflicts with older policy excerpts.\n10: - Receipts are required for every expense of $75.00 or more.\n11: - Expenses without required receipts are not reimbursable when a receipt is required.\n12: \n13: Air travel:\n14: \n15: - Economy airfare is reimbursable with a receipt.\n16: - Seat upgrades, extra-legroom fees, priority boarding, and similar optional upgrades are not reimbursable unless written preapproval is provided in the receipt evidence. No preapproval means no reimbursement.\n17: \n18: Lodging:\n19: \n20: - Lodging is reimbursable up to $220.00 per night, including room, taxes, and mandatory fees.\n21: - Apply the cap by multiplying covered nights by $220.00.\n22: \n23: Meals:\n24: \n25: - Meals are reimbursable at actual cost up to $65.00 per day.\n26: - Alcohol is not reimbursable and must be removed from meal receipts.\n27: \n28: Ride-share:\n29: \n30: - Ride-share base fare is reimbursable with a receipt.\n31: - Tips are reimbursable up to 20% of the base fare.\n32: - Any tip amount above 20% of the base fare is not reimbursable.\n33: \n34: Supplies:\n35: \n36: - Work supplies can be reimbursed only when a required receipt is provided and the business purpose is clear.\n37: \n38: Trip covered by this audit:\n39: \n40: - Employee: Jordan Lee\n41: - Trip dates: 2026-05-08 to 2026-05-10\n42: - Covered lodging nights: 2\n\n(End of file - total 42 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Current Finance Travel Policy\n\nPolicy date: 2026-04-20\n\nEffective for trips starting on or after 2026-05-01. This policy supersedes older travel policy excerpts for covered trips.\n\nGeneral rules:\n\n- Use this current policy when it conflicts with older policy excerpts.\n- Receipts are required for every expense of $75.00 or more.\n- Expenses without required receipts are not reimbursable when a receipt is required.\n\nAir travel:\n\n- Economy airfare is reimbursable with a receipt.\n- Seat upgrades, extra-legroom fees, priority boarding, and similar optional upgrades are not reimbursable unless written preapproval is provided in the receipt evidence. No preapproval means no reimbursement.\n\nLodging:\n\n- Lodging is reimbursable up to $220.00 per night, including room, taxes, and mandatory fees.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/current_policy.md","text":"# Current Finance Travel Policy\n\nPolicy date: 2026-04-20\n\nEffective for trips starting on or after 2026-05-01. This policy supersedes older travel policy excerpts for covered trips.\n\nGeneral rules:\n\n- Use this current policy when it conflicts with older policy excerpts.\n- Receipts are required for every expense of $75.00 or more.\n- Expenses without required receipts are not reimbursable when a receipt is required.\n\nAir travel:\n\n- Economy airfare is reimbursable with a receipt.\n- Seat upgrades, extra-legroom fees, priority boarding, and similar optional upgrades are not reimbursable unless written preapproval is provided in the receipt evidence. No preapproval means no reimbursement.\n\nLodging:\n\n- Lodging is reimbursable up to $220.00 per night, including room, taxes, and mandatory fees.\n- Apply the cap by multiplying covered nights by $220.00.\n\nMeals:\n\n- Meals are reimbursable at actual cost up to $65.00 per day.\n- Alcohol is not reimbursable and must be removed from meal receipts.\n\nRide-share:\n\n- Ride-share base fare is reimbursable with a receipt.\n- Tips are reimbursable up to 20% of the base fare.\n- Any tip amount above 20% of the base fare is not reimbursable.\n\nSupplies:\n\n- Work supplies can be reimbursed only when a required receipt is provided and the business purpose is clear.\n\nTrip covered by this audit:\n\n- Employee: Jordan Lee\n- Trip dates: 2026-05-08 to 2026-05-10\n- Covered lodging nights: 2","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":42,"totalLines":42,"truncated":false}},"title":"tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/current_policy.md","time":{"start":1790565218614,"end":1790565218645}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0dfa9c8d81067542016ab9db62790887d2943a9aee23ab2207"}},"id":"prt_0e600f933001kXRwgRkjSvILk9","sessionID":"ses_f19ff5269ffeWS83Lv5ueXIeyF","messageID":"msg_0e600e3b00019HCbG2WJIHoAWD"}}
