{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790565258682,"sessionID":"ses_f19ff5269ffeWS83Lv5ueXIeyF","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_2EJ17IbTnXGEnpfXio9sXWiR","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/policy_application.md\n+# Policy Application\n+\n+## Checkpoint 1 — Policy selection\n+\n+- **Trip audited:** Jordan Lee, 2026-05-08 through 2026-05-10; two covered lodging nights.\n+- **Controlling source:** Current Finance Travel Policy dated **2026-04-20**. It is effective for trips starting on or after 2026-05-01, and this trip starts 2026-05-08. The policy expressly supersedes older excerpts when they conflict. The 2026-03-01 stale excerpt therefore does not control.\n+\n+## Rules applied\n+\n+- **Receipt threshold:** Receipts are required for every expense of **$75.00 or more**. An expense without a required receipt is not reimbursable.\n+- **Seat upgrades:** Optional upgrades are not reimbursable unless written preapproval is included in the receipt evidence. T-002 has no written preapproval.\n+- **Lodging cap:** **$220.00 per covered night**, including room, taxes, and mandatory fees. For two covered nights, the cap is 2 × $220.00 = **$440.00**.\n+- **Meals and alcohol:** Meals reimburse at actual cost up to **$65.00 per day**. Alcohol is excluded and removed from the receipt calculation.\n+- **Ride-share tips:** Base fare is reimbursable with a receipt; tip reimbursement is capped at **20% of base fare**. Any tip above that is excluded.\n+- **Supplies receipts:** Work supplies require both a clear business purpose and a required receipt. T-006 has a clear purpose, but its $82.00 amount meets the receipt threshold and no receipt was provided, so it is not reimbursable.\n*** Add File: /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/expense_decisions.md\n+# Expense Decisions\n+\n+## Checkpoint 2 — Item-level audit\n+\n+| Expense ID | Claimed | Approved | Non-reimbursable | Status | Policy or receipt reason |\n+|---|---:|---:|---:|---|---|\n+| T-001 | $480.00 | $480.00 | $0.00 | approved | Economy airfare is reimbursable with a receipt; receipt is present. |\n+| T-002 | $45.00 | $0.00 | $45.00 | rejected | Exit-row seat upgrade is optional; no written preapproval is included. |\n+| T-003 | $510.00 | $440.00 | $70.00 | partial | Two covered nights × $220.00 lodging cap = $440.00; receipt is present. |\n+| T-004 | $76.00 | $58.00 | $18.00 | partial | Receipt shows $58.00 food and $18.00 wine. Alcohol is not reimbursable; eligible food is within the $65.00 daily meal cap. |\n+| T-005 | $70.00 | $60.00 | $10.00 | partial | Receipt shows $50.00 base fare and $20.00 tip. Tip cap is 20% × $50.00 = $10.00; approved total is $50.00 + $10.00. |\n+| T-006 | $82.00 | $0.00 | $82.00 | rejected | Clear business purpose (“USB-C adapters for demo room”), but $82.00 requires a receipt and none was provided. |\n+| T-007 | $18.00 | $18.00 | $0.00 | approved | Breakfast is within the $65.00 daily meal cap; receipt is present. |\n+\n+**Status definitions:** `approved` means the full claim is reimbursable; `partial` means some of the claim is reimbursable; `rejected` means none is reimbursable.\n*** Add File: /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/reimbursement_summary.md\n+# Reimbursement Summary\n+\n+## Checkpoint 3 — Reimbursement totals\n+\n+- **Reimbursable total: $1,056.00**\n+- **Non-reimbursable total: $225.00**\n+\n+Reimbursable arithmetic: $480.00 (T-001) + $0.00 (T-002) + $440.00 (T-003) + $58.00 (T-004) + $60.00 (T-005) + $0.00 (T-006) + $18.00 (T-007) = **$1,056.00**.\n+\n+Non-reimbursable arithmetic: $45.00 (T-002) + $70.00 (T-003) + $18.00 (T-004) + $10.00 (T-005) + $82.00 (T-006) = **$225.00**. Reconciliation: $1,056.00 + $225.00 = $1,281.00 total claimed.\n+\n+- **Fully approved:** T-001, T-007\n+- **Partially reimbursed or capped:** T-003, T-004, T-005\n+- **Rejected:** T-002, T-006\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/policy_application.md\nA tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/expense_decisions.md\nA tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/reimbursement_summary.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/policy_application.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/policy_application.md\n+++ /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/policy_application.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@\n+# Policy Application\n+\n+## Checkpoint 1 — Policy selection\n+\n+- **Trip audited:** Jordan Lee, 2026-05-08 through 2026-05-10; two covered lodging nights.\n+- **Controlling source:** Current Finance Travel Policy dated **2026-04-20**. It is effective for trips starting on or after 2026-05-01, and this trip starts 2026-05-08. The policy expressly supersedes older excerpts when they conflict. The 2026-03-01 stale excerpt therefore does not control.\n+\n+## Rules applied\n+\n+- **Receipt threshold:** Receipts are required for every expense of **$75.00 or more**. An expense without a required receipt is not reimbursable.\n+- **Seat upgrades:** Optional upgrades are not reimbursable unless written preapproval is included in the receipt evidence. T-002 has no written preapproval.\n+- **Lodging cap:** **$220.00 per covered night**, including room, taxes, and mandatory fees. For two covered nights, the cap is 2 × $220.00 = **$440.00**.\n+- **Meals and alcohol:** Meals reimburse at actual cost up to **$65.00 per day**. Alcohol is excluded and removed from the receipt calculation.\n+- **Ride-share tips:** Base fare is reimbursable with a receipt; tip reimbursement is capped at **20% of base fare**. Any tip above that is excluded.\n+- **Supplies receipts:** Work supplies require both a clear business purpose and a required receipt. T-006 has a clear purpose, but its $82.00 amount meets the receipt threshold and no receipt was provided, so it is not reimbursable.\n\nIndex: /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/expense_decisions.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/expense_decisions.md\n+++ /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/expense_decisions.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@\n+# Expense Decisions\n+\n+## Checkpoint 2 — Item-level audit\n+\n+| Expense ID | Claimed | Approved | Non-reimbursable | Status | Policy or receipt reason |\n+|---|---:|---:|---:|---|---|\n+| T-001 | $480.00 | $480.00 | $0.00 | approved | Economy airfare is reimbursable with a receipt; receipt is present. |\n+| T-002 | $45.00 | $0.00 | $45.00 | rejected | Exit-row seat upgrade is optional; no written preapproval is included. |\n+| T-003 | $510.00 | $440.00 | $70.00 | partial | Two covered nights × $220.00 lodging cap = $440.00; receipt is present. |\n+| T-004 | $76.00 | $58.00 | $18.00 | partial | Receipt shows $58.00 food and $18.00 wine. Alcohol is not reimbursable; eligible food is within the $65.00 daily meal cap. |\n+| T-005 | $70.00 | $60.00 | $10.00 | partial | Receipt shows $50.00 base fare and $20.00 tip. Tip cap is 20% × $50.00 = $10.00; approved total is $50.00 + $10.00. |\n+| T-006 | $82.00 | $0.00 | $82.00 | rejected | Clear business purpose (“USB-C adapters for demo room”), but $82.00 requires a receipt and none was provided. |\n+| T-007 | $18.00 | $18.00 | $0.00 | approved | Breakfast is within the $65.00 daily meal cap; receipt is present. |\n+\n+**Status definitions:** `approved` means the full claim is reimbursable; `partial` means some of the claim is reimbursable; `rejected` means none is reimbursable.\n\nIndex: /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/reimbursement_summary.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/reimbursement_summary.md\n+++ /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/reimbursement_summary.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@\n+# Reimbursement Summary\n+\n+## Checkpoint 3 — Reimbursement totals\n+\n+- **Reimbursable total: $1,056.00**\n+- **Non-reimbursable total: $225.00**\n+\n+Reimbursable arithmetic: $480.00 (T-001) + $0.00 (T-002) + $440.00 (T-003) + $58.00 (T-004) + $60.00 (T-005) + $0.00 (T-006) + $18.00 (T-007) = **$1,056.00**.\n+\n+Non-reimbursable arithmetic: $45.00 (T-002) + $70.00 (T-003) + $18.00 (T-004) + $10.00 (T-005) + $82.00 (T-006) = **$225.00**. Reconciliation: $1,056.00 + $225.00 = $1,281.00 total claimed.\n+\n+- **Fully approved:** T-001, T-007\n+- **Partially reimbursed or capped:** T-003, T-004, T-005\n+- **Rejected:** T-002, T-006\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/policy_application.md","relativePath":"tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/policy_application.md","type":"add","patch":"Index: /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/policy_application.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/policy_application.md\n+++ /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/policy_application.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@\n+# Policy Application\n+\n+## Checkpoint 1 — Policy selection\n+\n+- **Trip audited:** Jordan Lee, 2026-05-08 through 2026-05-10; two covered lodging nights.\n+- **Controlling source:** Current Finance Travel Policy dated **2026-04-20**. It is effective for trips starting on or after 2026-05-01, and this trip starts 2026-05-08. The policy expressly supersedes older excerpts when they