{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790565267425,"sessionID":"ses_f19ff5269ffeWS83Lv5ueXIeyF","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_RDXh6PJvM9wgPUQwtSpe0P3O","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/policy_application.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/policy_application.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Policy Application\n2: \n3: ## Checkpoint 1 — Policy selection\n4: \n5: - **Trip audited:** Jordan Lee, 2026-05-08 through 2026-05-10; two covered lodging nights.\n6: - **Controlling source:** Current Finance Travel Policy dated **2026-04-20**. It is effective for trips starting on or after 2026-05-01, and this trip starts 2026-05-08. The policy expressly supersedes older excerpts when they conflict. The 2026-03-01 stale excerpt therefore does not control.\n7: \n8: ## Rules applied\n9: \n10: - **Receipt threshold:** Receipts are required for every expense of **$75.00 or more**. An expense without a required receipt is not reimbursable.\n11: - **Seat upgrades:** Optional upgrades are not reimbursable unless written preapproval is included in the receipt evidence. T-002 has no written preapproval.\n12: - **Lodging cap:** **$220.00 per covered night**, including room, taxes, and mandatory fees. For two covered nights, the cap is 2 × $220.00 = **$440.00**.\n13: - **Meals and alcohol:** Meals reimburse at actual cost up to **$65.00 per day**. Alcohol is excluded and removed from the receipt calculation.\n14: - **Ride-share tips:** Base fare is reimbursable with a receipt; tip reimbursement is capped at **20% of base fare**. Any tip above that is excluded.\n15: - **Supplies receipts:** Work supplies require both a clear business purpose and a required receipt. T-006 has a clear purpose, but its $82.00 amount meets the receipt threshold and no receipt was provided, so it is not reimbursable.\n\n(End of file - total 15 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Policy Application\n\n## Checkpoint 1 — Policy selection\n\n- **Trip audited:** Jordan Lee, 2026-05-08 through 2026-05-10; two covered lodging nights.\n- **Controlling source:** Current Finance Travel Policy dated **2026-04-20**. It is effective for trips starting on or after 2026-05-01, and this trip starts 2026-05-08. The policy expressly supersedes older excerpts when they conflict. The 2026-03-01 stale excerpt therefore does not control.\n\n## Rules applied\n\n- **Receipt threshold:** Receipts are required for every expense of **$75.00 or more**. An expense without a required receipt is not reimbursable.\n- **Seat upgrades:** Optional upgrades are not reimbursable unless written preapproval is included in the receipt evidence. T-002 has no written preapproval.\n- **Lodging cap:** **$220.00 per covered night**, including room, taxes, and mandatory fees. For two covered nights, the cap is 2 × $220.00 = **$440.00**.\n- **Meals and alcohol:** Meals reimburse at actual cost up to **$65.00 per day**. Alcohol is excluded and removed from the receipt calculation.\n- **Ride-share tips:** Base fare is reimbursable with a receipt; tip reimbursement is capped at **20% of base fare**. Any tip above that is excluded.\n- **Supplies receipts:** Work supplies require both a clear business purpose and a required receipt. T-006 has a clear purpose, but its $82.00 amount meets the receipt threshold and no receipt was provided, so it is not reimbursable.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/policy_application.md","text":"# Policy Application\n\n## Checkpoint 1 — Policy selection\n\n- **Trip audited:** Jordan Lee, 2026-05-08 through 2026-05-10; two covered lodging nights.\n- **Controlling source:** Current Finance Travel Policy dated **2026-04-20**. It is effective for trips starting on or after 2026-05-01, and this trip starts 2026-05-08. The policy expressly supersedes older excerpts when they conflict. The 2026-03-01 stale excerpt therefore does not control.\n\n## Rules applied\n\n- **Receipt threshold:** Receipts are required for every expense of **$75.00 or more**. An expense without a required receipt is not reimbursable.\n- **Seat upgrades:** Optional upgrades are not reimbursable unless written preapproval is included in the receipt evidence. T-002 has no written preapproval.\n- **Lodging cap:** **$220.00 per covered night**, including room, taxes, and mandatory fees. For two covered nights, the cap is 2 × $220.00 = **$440.00**.\n- **Meals and alcohol:** Meals reimburse at actual cost up to **$65.00 per day**. Alcohol is excluded and removed from the receipt calculation.\n- **Ride-share tips:** Base fare is reimbursable with a receipt; tip reimbursement is capped at **20% of base fare**. Any tip above that is excluded.\n- **Supplies receipts:** Work supplies require both a clear business purpose and a required receipt. T-006 has a clear purpose, but its $82.00 amount meets the receipt threshold and no receipt was provided, so it is not reimbursable.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":15,"totalLines":15,"truncated":false}},"title":"tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/policy_application.md","time":{"start":1790565267400,"end":1790565267423}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0d9917304ef2a2c1016ab9db934df887d2a4d1148630f12672"}},"id":"prt_0e601b7a3001hvftdDWpzwq5M2","sessionID":"ses_f19ff5269ffeWS83Lv5ueXIeyF","messageID":"msg_0e601a355001jSsrr2BqWHUl76"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790565267425,"sessionID":"ses_f19ff5269ffeWS83Lv5ueXIeyF","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_x7IGR3b2pFP31bRKVKqIYcqg","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/expense_decisions.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/expense_decisions.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Expense Decisions\n2: \n3: ## Checkpoint 2 — Item-level audit\n4: \n5: | Expense ID | Claimed | Approved | Non-reimbursable | Status | Policy or receipt reason |\n6: |---|---:|---:|---:|---|---|\n7: | T-001 | $480.00 | $480.00 | $0.00 | approved | Economy airfare is reimbursable with a receipt; receipt is present. |\n8: | T-002 | $45.00 | $0.00 | $45.00 | rejected | Exit-row seat upgrade is optional; no written preapproval is included. |\n9: | T-003 | $510.00 | $440.00 | $70.00 | partial | Two covered nights × $220.00 lodging cap = $440.00; receipt is present. |\n10: | T-004 | $76.00 | $58.00 | $18.00 | partial | Receipt shows $58.00 food and $18.00 wine. Alcohol is not reimbursable; eligible food is within the $65.00 daily meal cap. |\n11: | T-005 | $70.00 | $60.00 | $10.00 | partial | Receipt shows $50.00 base fare and $20.00 tip. Tip cap is 20% × $50.00 = $10.00; approved total is $50.00 + $10.00. |\n12: | T-006 | $82.00 | $0.00 | $82.00 | rejected | Clear business purpose (“USB-C adapters for demo room”), but $82.00 requires a receipt and none was provided. |\n13: | T-007 | $18.00 | $18.00 | $0.00 | approved | Breakfast is within the $65.00 daily meal cap; receipt is present. |\n14: \n15: **Status definitions:** `approved` means the full claim is reimbursable; `partial` means some of the claim is reimbursable; `rejected` means none is reimbursable.\n\n(End of file - total 15 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Expense Decisions\n\n## Checkpoint 2 — Item-level audit\n\n| Expense ID | Claimed | Approved | Non-reimbursable | Status | Policy or receipt reason |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---|---|\n| T-001 | $480.00 | $480.00 | $0.00 | approved | Economy airfare is reimbursable with a receipt; receipt is present. |\n| T-002 | $45.00 | $0.00 | $45.00 | rejected | Exit-row seat upgrade is optional; no written preapproval is included. |\n| T-003 | $510.00 | $440.00 | $70.00 | partial | Two covered nights × $220.00 lodging cap = $440.00; receipt is present. |\n| T-004 | $76.00 | $58.00 | $18.00 | partial | Receipt shows $58.00 food and $18.00 wine. Alcohol is not reimbursable; eligible food is within the $65.00 daily meal cap. |\n| T-005 | $70.00 | $60.00 | $10.00 | partial | Receipt shows $50.00 base fare and $20.00 tip. Tip cap is 20% × $50.00 = $10.00; approved total is $50.00 + $10.00. |\n| T-006 | $82.00 | $0.00 | $82.00 | rejected | Clear business purpose (“USB-C adapters for demo room”), but $82.00 requires a receipt and none was provided. |\n| T-007 | $18.00 | $18.00 | $0.00 | approved | Breakfast is within the $65.00 daily meal cap; receipt is present. |\n\n**Status definitions:** `approved` means the full claim is reimbursable; `partial` means some of the claim is reimbursable; `rejected` means none is reimbursable.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/expense_decisions.md","text":"# Expense Decisions\n\n## Checkpoint 2 — Item-level audit\n\n| Expense ID | Claimed | Approved | Non-reimbursable | Status | Policy or receipt reason |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---|---|\n| T-001 | $480.00 | $480.00 | $0.00 | approved | Economy airfare is reimbursable with a receipt; receipt is present. |\n| T-002 | $45.00 | $0.00 | $45.00 | rejected | Exit-row seat upgrade is optional; no written preapproval is included. |\n| T-003 | $510.00 | $440.00 | $70.00 | partial | Two covered nights × $220.00 lodging cap = $440.00; receipt is present. |\n| T-004 | $76.00 | $58.00 | $18.00 | partial | Receipt shows $58.00 food and $18.00 wine. Alcohol is not reimbursable; eligible food is within the $65.00 daily meal cap. |\n| T-005 | $70.00 | $60.00 | $10.00 | partial | Receipt shows $50.00 base fare and $20.00 tip. Tip cap is 20% × $50.00 = $10.00; approved total is $50.00 + $10.00. |\n| T-006 | $82.00 | $0.00 | $82.00 | rejected | Clear business purpose (“USB-C adapters for demo room”), but $82.00 requires a receipt and none was provided. |\n| T-007 | $18.00 | $18.00 | $0.00 | approved | Breakfast is within the $65.00 daily meal cap; receipt is present. |\n\n**Status definitions:** `approved` means the full claim is reimbursable; `partial` means some of the claim is reimbursable; `rejected` means none is reimbursable.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":15,"totalLines":15,"truncated":false}},"title":"tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/expense_decisions.md","time":{"start":1790565267419,"end":1790565267424}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0d9917304ef2a2c1016ab9db934e1087d2a82553f8d2b667fb"}},"id":"prt_0e601b7d30013Xi3wChVl10jCi","sessionID":"ses_f19ff5269ffeWS83Lv5ueXIeyF","messageID":"msg_0e601a355001jSsrr2BqWHUl76"}}
